    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high 81.88 efficiency score. With a favorable matchup against the hittable Bryce Elder (4.33 xERA), **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an aggressive park factor and dynamic platoon positioning in the three-hole. Following closely, **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) provide high-floor production at the top of the order. **Sam Antonacci**, in particular, leverages a significant SP skill advantage against Hunter Brown, while **Drake Baldwin** capitalizes on an elite ballpark environment, making them the engines of our daily output.\n\nTactical adjustments remain key as we navigate a high volume of \"Lineup Pending\" statuses. **Heliot Ramos** (65.86) is a high-upside play today, bolstered by favorable wind conditions that offset the risk of facing a high-velocity catcher, while **Jackson Merrill** (60.12) earns his spot specifically for his stolen base potential against a pitcher with a slow delivery. The most difficult bench decision involved **Curtis Mead**, who nearly cracked the lineup with a 55.76 score against Bratt. Ultimately, **Curtis Mead** was sidelined because his platoon disadvantage against the lefty starter dragged his efficiency below the thresholds set by **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo**, both of whom are projected to offer more consistent utility across our 5x5 categories today.\n\nWe must monitor the confirmed lineups closely, as many projections for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Dominic Smith** rely on assumed batting order placements. While the offensive outlook is strong, we remain cautious regarding the matchup for **Kyle Tucker** (51.42), whose score remains tempered by a challenging outing against Nolan McLean. All starters have been optimized for their specific scoring category contributions, but keep a close watch on potential rain or late-scratch announcements that could necessitate a pivot to **Brayan Rocchio** or **Denzer Guzman** from the bench.",
